`zassert_str_equal` and `strstr` functions expect null-terminated strings. The `test_common_cb`, `test_header_field_cb`, and `test_header_value_cb` functions copy data into `response_buf` but do not null-terminate it. This can lead to assertion failures or crashes when these functions are used with non-null-terminated data.

The fix is to explicitly null-terminate `response_buf` after the HTTP request has completed and all data has been copied by the callbacks, but before the assertions that rely on null-termination are made. This ensures that string comparison and search functions operate on valid, null-terminated strings.

